WEBVTT

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.680
Hiromi, I'll lead the group.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.980
Let Sandy block the wind for you.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:17.740
Sandy!

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.190
Sandy has a lot of energy.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.530
Yeah.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.830
Girls, the teacher's not here, but let's 
do our best to reach Misaki together.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.790
Okay.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.730
Passing on your right.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:32.400
What?

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.180
Tomo-chan, did you see that?

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.130
Those were women.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.340
They were riding really fast.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.130
Come to think of it, I think they passed us 
on our way to the entrance ceremony, too.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.450
Yeah.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.910
Those women just passed me.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:51.650
What?

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:55.510
Touring is nice, but I'd like 
to enjoy some speed, too.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.080
With the geared bicycle I'm riding today,
I can catch up to them!

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.400
Hiromi, let's go!

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.850
Let's go after them together!

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:06.570
What?

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.140
Here we go!

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.000
Really?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.280
Let's go!

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.960
W-Wait!

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.740
W-Wait, Hiromi! Sandy!

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.970
Wait!

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:53.710
Kano!

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:54.860
Yeah?

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.030
Someone's coming up behind us.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:57.690
What?

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.030
Those girls...

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.280
Wait, Sandy!

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:10.250
<b>#11 Bicycles Are Strange</b>

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.090
Huh? What's this?

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.160
We're pedaling so hard,
but we're not getting any closer.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.800
In fact, are we falling farther behind?

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:23.260
Oh, right. They're way, way faster than us.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.930
I wonder if I can go faster.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.920
Maybe if I pedal harder...

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.910
Sandy, I want to test 
how fast my bike can go!

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.120
Great idea! Let's try it!

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.190
Here we go, Unico!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.060
Full speed...

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.170
...ahead!

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.920
Let's go!

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.520
They're gone.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.990
What should we do?

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:15.640
This coastal road takes 
us straight to Misaki.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.730
But if they go down a different road...

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.320
L-Let's go after them.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.280
Oh, those two are still keeping up.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.380
That's Maiharu Hiromi-san,
the winner of the recent criterium.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.540
Now that you mention it, I do recognize her.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:37.370
But she'll exhaust herself in 
a second, pedaling like that.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.550
Let's give her some advice.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.760
All right! Let's show them
how to ride a bike.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.830
Full speed! Full speed!

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.930
Hello.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:54.030
I heard you're the Minami 
Kamakura Bicycle Club.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.190
What? Oh, yeah.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:55.960
That's us.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.260
It looks like you're trying to 
go fast, but you're pretty slow.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:01.230
What?

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.640
Even though we're pedaling so hard?

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.450
We'll show you how to ride a road racer.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:06.860
What?

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.400
I'm coming in behind you.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.330
What?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.320
Wh-What is this?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.790
Face forward!

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.570
First, leave a little more space between 
yourself and the bike in front of you.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:21.870
It's dangerous to stick too close together 
on public roads until you get used to it.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:25.190
There's no telling what 
might jump into the roadway.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.700
Safety first. Caution does no harm.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.300
Pushing yourself too hard causes accidents.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.350
O-Okay.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.180
Then there's your pedaling.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:33.930
My pedaling?

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.670
You're pedaling too recklessly.

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:39.980
Since you're pushing yourselves 
to your limit, it's dangerous.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.900
You shouldn't ride so fast without 
giving yourself some breathing room.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:47.050
And trying to power through is ineffective.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:50.560
Always pay attention to the condition 
of yourself, your bike, and the ground.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.740
Make sure you're in control.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.550
Control?

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:57.770
You mean it's not enough for me 
to just do my best with my bike?

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.330
Trying hard is a good thing.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.810
But you have to expend that effort well.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:04.460
Try doing as I say.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.170
Okay.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.890
First, relax and bend your elbows slightly.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:12.880
You need to relax your upper body 
so your legs have more power.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:17.740
Arch your back like you're carrying 
a balloon in front of your stomach.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.000
Like this?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:19.520
That's it.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.100
Then breathe in and out. How does that feel?

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.840
It's easier to breathe.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:25.850
Right?

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.490
It's a lot easier to pedal now.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.150
No fair. Hiromi's getting all the lectures.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:33.450
Whoa. You can speak Japanese?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.790
Yes, I'm fluent.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:39.590
Pedal, pedal.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:43.190
Do you usually stand while pedaling uphill?

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.880
Yeah, it's easier.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.320
Maybe, but you shouldn't do it all the time.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:54.430
It may feel easier to pedal while 
standing while going uphill,

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:59.900
but since it uses your body weight and 
your entire body's muscles at once,

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.250
it's a powerful but exhausting technique.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.440
Oh, no. Really?

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.790
So it's important to know when to use it.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:11.360
Try to remain sitting even 
while going uphill and

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.570
focus on turning the pedals 
as much as possible.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:18.680
Come to think of it, Shiki-sensei 
mentioned turning the pedals

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.540
during the criterium, too.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:23.900
What? But we're already turning them.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.510
What does that mean?

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:32.460
Instead of relying on strength,
keep your ankles steady and pedal smoothly.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.890
Switch to a lighter gear

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:38.320
and try pedaling with the base of your 
big toe on the axis of the pedal.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:42.200
You'll be able to pedal 
at a consistent cadence.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.810
Wow, I feel like it's easier to pedal now.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.020
Yeah.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.630
When you accelerate,
gradually increase your speed.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:53.280
It'll prevent you from getting exhausted 
and allow you to ride for longer.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.620
I see.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:01.080
Focus on your pedaling and follow us.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.240
Okay!

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:06.620
Where on earth did they go?

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.330
And where are we?

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.720
What is this place?

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.760
Let's check.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:16.260
Oh, no. We made a wrong turn somewhere.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.060
We're off the prefectural highway.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.470
What? When?

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.560
Is there any way we can meet up with them?

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.790
What should we do?

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:27.860
That's it.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.990
<b>Uraga
Ferry</b>

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:38.870
This is easier than before.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:42.450
Yeah. I don't feel as tired anymore.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.840
Looks like you're keeping up.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:46.750
You can go at your own pace.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.090
Okay.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.530
By the way, the other girls haven't kept up.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:52.880
Are they are okay?

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:54.300
What?

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.350
We left the others behind!

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.150
They're not coming.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:07.620
But this is the way to Misaki.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.480
I wonder where they are right now.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.410
Oh, right. I can call them.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.780
There they are!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.700
Hiromi! Sandy!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.910
Girls!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.830
Hey!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.190
What are you girls doing over there?

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.520
That's amazing.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.360
Did you teleport?

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.800
Yeah, more or less.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.180
We actually rode over on that.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.460
A boat?

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.020
Really? I didn't know 
there was a ferry there.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.590
I'm glad we found you.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:50.860
I know. I don't know what we 
would've done if we hadn't.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.730
Sorry, everyone.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.230
I'll be careful from now on.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.320
Nice to meet you again. I'm Hibara Kano.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.830
I was the host at the 
criterium the other day.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.360
Do you remember me?

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:08.170
You're right.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.640
We meet again.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:12.490
I'm Karino Rinko.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.170
That's Oshino Riri.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:20.090
We're members of SOUND-C,
the Mimami Kamakura FM station's team.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.150
You're professionals?

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.560
No wonder you're fast.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.780
We're not professionals, but a business team.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.560
It's like a club for adults.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.240
Really? A business...

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:34.400
Huh?

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.280
Hiromi? Are you okay?

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.110
Huh?

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.900
What's wrong?

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.740
I-I need to sit...

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.080
This way.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.760
Hiromi, are you okay?

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:48.040
I wonder what happened.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.330
I suddenly felt light-headed.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.200
Are you anemic?

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.270
Do you feel weak?

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.760
Yeah, something like that.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:58.980
Could it be...

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:01.340
Did you have a proper breakfast?

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:05.430
Come to think of it, you said 
all you had to eat was yogurt.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:07.760
So you were riding without 
eating anything first?

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.180
You can't do that.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.270
Eat this, too.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.030
It's so sweet!

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:26.390
I like sweet things,
but this seems too sweet.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.670
Quit complaining and drink up!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:28.610
Okay!

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.780
Why did this happen to her?

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:34.500
It's not anemia, is it?

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:37.080
It's called "hitting the wall."

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.760
Simply put, she's out of energy.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:44.720
<b>Blood
Sugar</b>

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:44.720
Exercising lowered her blood sugar, 
so she couldn't move anymore.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.300
A bicycle's engine is the person pedaling it.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:54.220
Riding without eating is like trying 
to drive a car without any gas.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:56.410
It's no wonder she couldn't move anymore.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.820
It's not good for you either, so be careful.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.830
How do you feel? Try standing.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.600
I think I'm feeling better.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.610
Are you okay, Hiromi?

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.290
Yeah, I feel steadier.

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:19.300
That jelly and soda gave me tons of energy.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.970
It's the electrolytes and sugar.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.970
Carbonated beverages have 
lots of sugar in them.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.710
I don't really understand, but it's amazing.

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:30.140
Thank you for your help, Hibara-san.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:32.170
That was just a stop-gap.

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.730
Make sure you eat a proper meal, too.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:35.600
Okay.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:39.980
Well, we're heading toward Chiba now.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.190
You can get there from here?

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:45.980
See you later.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:47.470
Goodbye.

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.870
Thank you.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.590
I'm glad we met such nice people.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:56.810
I know.

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:59.970
I hope we can be like them someday.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.720
Yeah. They were so cool.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.720
Let's get Hiromi something to eat.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.680
Hooray! Food, food!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.750
Let's replenish our blood sugar!

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.320
Wow.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.780
Could I get this on a boat?

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.610
Not right now.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.530
Why don't we get some fish over there?

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.530
<b>Fried
Tuna
Skewers</b>

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.410
<b>Black Ship
Croquettes</b>

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:44.510
Okay.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:48.150
We filled our stomachs and 
we're almost halfway there.

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:50.600
Let's do it. No more splitting up.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.250
Okay.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.050
You're still eating?

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.720
It's a long hill.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.060
Good luck.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.270
Thank you.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:35.260
Look. You can see all of 
the Miura Peninsula from here.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.640
Is this a farm?

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:42.980
Yeah. They grow Miura radishes 
here during the winter.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.730
You can see Mt. Fuji from here, too.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:46.360
You're right.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:49.890
What are those? Windmills?

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:51.390
Yeah.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:55.960
They have wind farms in Miura Peninsula, huh?

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.890
Let's go there next.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:01.920
Sounds good. I want to see 
the windmills up close.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.320
I'd like to see them, too.

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:06.170
Since they're on the way, that sounds nice.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:09.800
Then let's head for the windmills!

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.010
How did we end up at the lighthouse?

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:15.890
Sorry. We took a wrong turn.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:19.610
You really can't read a map, can you?

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:20.680
What should we do?

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.810
Which way should we go?

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:26.260
It's okay. We can go this way.

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:28.020
Hey, you two!

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:29.610
No wandering off!

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.100
Are we at the windmills yet?

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.940
You can do it, Fuyune-san.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.620
Oh, no. What is this?

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:44.690
A flat tire, huh?

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:46.680
What? But this was expensive.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.590
How'd I get a flat?

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.620
I don't think price has much to do with it.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.880
What should we do?

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:56.550
I'm the only one who can't keep going.

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.920
We'll have to call the teacher.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:03.780
Yeah. We made it this far on our own, but...

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:10.240
Wait. We can fix this easily.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.420
Really?

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.200
I brought a spare tube.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.210
That should do it.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.220
Are you done?

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.200
Did you fix it, Natsumi?

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:35.680
Trying riding it, Fuyune-san.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.180
Okay.

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:41.520
It's working!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:43.160
That's great.

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.940
Natsumi-chan, that's amazing.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.560
Thanks, Natsumi.

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.150
Now I can ride with everyone else.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.220
Yeah.

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:54.080
Okay, let's head toward the windmills again!

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.660
They should be coming into view soon.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.510
Girls, it's the windmills!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.550
Where?

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:16.050
See?

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:34.180
We're here!

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.460
We did it.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:36.300
Yeah.

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.460
The wind feels nice.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:43.650
It's like it's blowing my 
exhaustion away with it.

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:44.580
Yeah.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:51.500
We're here. We made it here 
together on our bikes.

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:58.520
<i>Bicycles are strange.</i>

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:02.820
<i>Once you start riding,
 you don't think about going back.</i>

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.440
<i>If you keep pedaling,
you'll reach your destination.</i>

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.940
Just three kilometers left!

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.520
<i>Hills are hard,</i>

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.270
It's the last spurt, girls!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:14.700
<i>but once you see the view from the top 
of the hill, your fatigue disappears.</i>

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.610
Okay!

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:18.820
<i>Even if you encounter 
problems on a long ride,</i>

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:21.540
<i>you can keep going as long 
as your friends are with you.</i>

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:24.180
<i>As long as we're together,</i>

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:27.150
<i>we can overcome the assignments 
given to us by our teacher.</i>

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:32.160
<i>Since encountering bicycles,
I've experienced so many strange feelings.</i>

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:40.140
<i>There's still a lot I don't know, 
but there is one thing I do know.</i>

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:42.300
One kilometer left!

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.790
Yeah!

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:47.040
Jogashima Ohashi Bridge Toll Booth

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.070
Girls!

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.870
Shiki-sensei!

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.400
Goal!

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:09.460
Good work, everyone.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:13.040
Sensei, we made it.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.160
We did it.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:14.650
Yeah.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:19.150
I want to keep riding my bike to all 
kinds of places with all of you.

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:20.800
So do I, Hiromi.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:22.280
Me, too!

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:40.160
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.220
<i>A-O-P: The first cycling club.</i>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Kamakura Cycling</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Enoshima</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Shichirigahama</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Enoshima Line</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Kamakura Station</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Yokosuka Line</b>

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:47.220
<i>We're heading for Enoshima while 
making stops along the way</i>

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:49.290
<i>in our first cycling tour of Kamakura.</i>

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.800
<i>Last time we rode through town 
while being blown by the sea breeze</i>

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:57.080
<i>and enjoyed exquisite 
sweets at a seaside cafe.</i>

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.910
<i>Now, we're finally heading toward Enoshima.</i>

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:03.210
<b>Kamakura Cycling</b>

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:03.210
<b>Enoshima</b>

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:03.210
<b>Shichirigahama</b>

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:03.210
<b>Enoshima Line</b>

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:05.570
<i>But first...</i>

00:22:05.570 --> 00:22:08.430
Before we go to Enoshima,
there's someplace I want to stop by first.

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:09.680
What is it?

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:10.580
Let's go.

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:11.850
Okay, here we go.

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:14.220
I wonder what it is.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:18.410
<i>We're making a stop near 
Kamakura High School Station.</i>

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:21.500
Stop.

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:22.070
Okay.

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:22.950
This is it.

00:22:25.680 --> 00:22:28.950
This is that famous place.

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:27.290
That's right.

00:22:27.910 --> 00:22:29.610
It's the view.

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:34.290
<i>This is a popular spot where you can 
photograph the Enoshima train with</i>

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:35.670
<i>Shonan Beach in the background.</i>

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:38.040
<i>It appears in numerous anime and</i>

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:41.080
<i>is famously revered for 
shows about young adults.</i>

00:22:42.780 --> 00:22:44.640
I wanted to see this.

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:46.620
Yeah, definitely.

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:50.630
<i>Now that we've made our 
pilgrimage to the revered site,</i>

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:52.110
<i>it's time to keep heading toward Enoshima.</i>

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.810
I can see Enoshima.

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:57.240
Wow.

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:01.020
It takes no time to get 
to Enoshima on a bike.

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:02.270
And it feels great.

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:04.270
Yeah. I'm hungry.

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:05.420
Me, too.

00:23:05.420 --> 00:23:06.330
Yeah.

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:07.820
Lunch, lunch.

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:12.880
<i>We've arrived at Enoshima, a place about 
eight kilometers from Kamakura Station.</i>

00:23:10.050 --> 00:23:13.870
<b>Enoshima</b>

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:16.830
<b>Established 1909
Enoshima-tei</b>

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:17.420
<i>We're here to eat the famous Enoshima Bowl.</i>

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:26.630
<b>Famous Enoshima Bowl
 ¥1,100 (includes tax)
 *As of February 2017</b>

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:22.020
<i>Made with locally-caught horned turban mixed 
with eggs, it's an exquisite rice bowl.</i>

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:27.330
It's good.

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:27.740
Yeah.

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:32.210
The cycling's fun, and we 
get to eat lots of good food, too.

00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:32.810
Yeah.

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:34.050
Everything is great.

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:34.930
Yeah.

